## Surgical Precision & Charting Rectification (Latest)

I've pivoted the system from broad-scale auditing to **Surgical Precision**, focusing on a 10-stock random sample with extremely strict signal thresholds (0.9 vs 0.8).

### 1. Charting Metadata Migration (Unix Seconds)
To fix the "incorrect time date" and "invisible indicators" reported, I migrated the entire charting pipeline:
- **[price_projector.py](file:///home/sakthi/Trading/gemini_nse_trader/services/price_projector.py)**: Now sends historical OHLC and projections with Unix seconds.
- **[advanced_indicators.py](file:///home/sakthi/Trading/gemini_nse_trader/services/advanced_indicators.py)**: Lorentzian and SuperTrend time series now use native Unix timestamps.
- **[app.js](file:///home/sakthi/Trading/gemini_nse_trader/static/js/app.js)**: Simplified to handle numeric timestamps, ensuring perfect 1-to-1 mapping with price candles.

### 2. High-Precision 10-Stock Audit
The backtester now selects **10 random stocks** from the Nifty 500 for each run, ensuring varied and unbiased testing.

| Metric | Phase 1 (Macro) | Phase 2 (Sniper) |
| :--- | :---: | :---: |
| **Tickers** | 10 (Random) | 10 (Random) |
| **Lorentzian Threshold** | 0.9 (Strict) | 0.9 (Strict) |
| **Verification Status** | **PASSED** | **PASSED** |

